duckdb-fdw (2.0.1+git20260529.9354241-1PGSTY) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upgrade to the duckdb_fdw 2.0.1 main snapshot at 9354241
  * Switch from the SQLite compatibility layer to the native DuckDB C API
  * Build and run against the standalone libduckdb 1.5.5 package
  * Preserve the upstream 1.4.1 to 2.0.1 extension migration chain
  * Fix the 1.4.1 to 2.0.0 migration for supported PostgreSQL syntax
  * Do not install a private libduckdb.so into PostgreSQL's library directory
  * Remove the private-library RPATH so the standalone runtime is authoritative
  * Preserve legacy servers without user mappings and harden error cleanup
  * Keep scalar aggregate results in native DuckDB types for safe conversion
  * Align regression expectations with the current insert-only FDW callback policy

 -- Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0800

duckdb-fdw (1.4.3-1PGSTY) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase to duckdb_fdw main at 870bc43
  * Pin build headers to DuckDB 1.4.3 from pg_duckdb 1.1.1
  * Reuse libduckdb.so shipped by postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-duckdb
  * Patch sqlite3_api_wrapper.cpp for DuckDB 1.4.3 compatibility
  * Stop installing a second copy of libduckdb.so from duckdb_fdw
  * Drop the legacy x86_64 _GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0 override

